    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is anchored today by **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Gunnar Henderson** (71.25), who represent our strongest statistical plays. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a highly favorable matchup against McGreevy, where his ability to capitalize on a RHP/LHH platoon edge is bolstered by a leadoff spot that maximizes his chances for R and SB production. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** remains an elite start despite facing a southpaw; his projection is heavily buoyed by an ideal hitter's park and a dynamic platoon profile that survives the SP skill penalty. **Coby Mayo** (65.57) also earns a high-confidence start, as the park factor and positive platoon dynamics against Lopez create an efficiency profile that far exceeds his base projections.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Heliot Ramos** (45.53), who sat on the cusp of the lineup. While **Heliot Ramos** offered some intrigue due to favorable wind conditions, he ultimately fell short behind **Andy Pages** and **Kyle Tucker** because his matchup against the RHP Mlodzinski yielded a lower total expected output. We are also closely monitoring the high-end risks associated with facing top-tier arms like Sale; despite the talent level of **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages**, their daily efficiency scores have been compressed by Sale\u2019s elite sub-3.00 xERA. Owners should track lineup confirmations closely, as any shift in order for **Drake Baldwin** or **Nasim Nunez** could further pressure their marginal efficiency scores.",
